comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:41:47.927Z","harness:claude-code","Sibling class measured 2026-07-29 in the same record this item censuses: the author field of the same 41,021 entries holds 477 distinct spellings with no enumeration, no contract entry and no gate, and four of its six most frequent values are two harnesses written two ways. It is the same ungoverned-value-domain shape as the 71 op literals, one layer harder for the same reason - the stream is append-only, so neither vocabulary can be fixed by migration and both need read-time canonicalization against declared data. Owner for the author half is pm-3yxwv5; keep the two separate because the op vocabulary is written only by the product while the author vocabulary is also written by callers through --author and PM_AUTHOR."
  "2026-08-01T09:52:05.174Z","harness:claude-code","Live op census, 2026-08-01, over all 2,258 history streams and 42,771 entries. 37 distinct op literals are actually written: update 10,931, comment_add 8,010, files_add 6,592, tests_add 3,086, claim 2,745, release 2,281, create 2,215, close 2,202, docs_add 1,431, test_run_track 913, note_add 725, learning_add 636, update_audit 309, update_ownership_bypass 120, append 115, plan_complete_step 85, plan_add_step 71, plan_update_step 44, history_repair 42, history_compact_baseline 41, history_compact 41, history_redact 23, plan_create_metadata 19, history:author-acknowledge 9, plan_create_initial_step 12, plan_append_discovery 12, delete 12, plan_append_validation 9, plan_append_decision 7, plan_approve 6, plan_link_step 4, comment_edit 4, comment_delete 3, plan_unlink_step 1, plan_reorder_step 1, note_delete 1. The naming-convention finding is confirmed and is now a single outlier: history:author-acknowledge is the one colon-namespaced literal in the entire immutable record; every other op is snake_case, and the plan_* family is the one that uses a namespace prefix without a separator. That makes the canonicalization tractable -- one recorded spelling has to move, not a class of them. The gap between 37 written and ~71 declared is also the measurement pm-pww8ax needs: half the declared vocabulary has never been exercised on a real workspace."
body: ""
